  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 300 AM MST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nDrier air will move in Tuesday morning, bringing an end to \nprecipitation, though the end time has slightly slowed compared to \nprevious forecasts. While not nearly as strong as Monday, breezy to \nwindy northwest winds are expected to continue into Tuesday with \nhighs rebounding to near seasonal averages. Look for plentiful \nsunshine to return to the area Tuesday as well. \n\nMid-week and beyond, ridging will try to build back in over the \nregion, but a few moisture starved upper level lows will hamper a \npotential warming trend. Overall, temperatures are expected to \nremain fairly close to seasonal averages during this period. \nConditions look generally dry too, though a compact upper level low \npassing through Wednesday may bring a few rain and/or high elevation \nsnow showers. Expect winds to be light Wednesday through Friday, but \na few ensemble members show stronger winds moving into the area\nwith an upper level low passing north of us over the weekend.",
